{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l2rmnzjw","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"electrochemistry","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","topic":"conductance-and-electrolysis","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pagnosub3subaq-was-added-to-an-aqueous-kcl-solutio-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-kofhv7mptmuje8yi","content":"<p>AgNO<sub>3</sub>(aq.) was added to an aqueous KCl solution gradually and the conductivity of the solution was measured. The plot of conductance (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.57ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 694 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"39B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-39B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) versus the volume of AgNO<sub>3</sub> is</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m03tmk82/23ae5773-0525-484f-8cf6-3b03a8939bce/9db73c20-5fb7-11ef-86b4-fd90d6602aa3/file-jaoe38c1m03tmk83.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1m03tmk82/23ae5773-0525-484f-8cf6-3b03a8939bce/9db73c20-5fb7-11ef-86b4-fd90d6602aa3/file-jaoe38c1m03tmk83.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Electrochemistry Question 21 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m03tmk82/23ae5773-0525-484f-8cf6-3b03a8939bce/9db73c20-5fb7-11ef-86b4-fd90d6602aa3/file-jaoe38c1m03tmk83.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m03tmk82/23ae5773-0525-484f-8cf6-3b0